  "title": "Amundsen reaches the South Pole",
  "summary": "Norwegian explorer Roald Amundsen and four companions reached the geographic South Pole on 14 December 1911, five weeks before Robert Falcon Scott's party. They travelled with dogs from the base Framheim on the Bay of Whales. The round trip took 99 days and covered about 3,000 km.",
